  "result": {
    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.trophic_differences - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.trophic_differences.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.trophic_differences()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get the trophic level difference across every edge.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.trophic_differences()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get the trophic level difference across every edge.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.trophic_differences()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Get the trophic level difference across every edge.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nGet the trophic level difference across every edge.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L60669-L60757){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.trophic_differences(weighted=None)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Trophic differences](../assets/graphs/trophic-differences.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The same food web, laid out by trophic level, with each edge labelled by the level of the predator minus the level of the prey. Mouse to owl jumps 1.5 levels and is drawn in accent, fox to owl only 0.5, and the other four edges exactly 1.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nFor each edge from `u` to `v`, the difference `level(v) - level(u)` between the trophic\nlevels of its endpoints (see `trophic_levels()`). In a perfectly layered network every\ndifference is exactly 1; differences far from 1 mark edges that skip levels (an\nomnivore eating at several levels) or run \"backwards\" against the hierarchy.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether trophic levels weight diets by edge weight. If `None` (default), follows the\n    graph.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [dict[int, float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A dictionary mapping edge IDs to level differences.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   As for `trophic_levels()`.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~trophic_levels`) \n\n:   The node levels behind the differences.\n\n[](`~trophic_incoherence_parameter`) \n\n:   The spread of the differences.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThe owl's two meals differ: the edge from the mouse jumps 1.5 levels, the edge from the\nfox only 0.5. The differences are keyed by edge ID, so they can be stored as an edge\nattribute:\n\n::: {#56b5f029 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nweb = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"grass\", \"rabbit\"), (\"grass\", \"mouse\"), (\"rabbit\", \"fox\"),\n     (\"mouse\", \"fox\"), (\"mouse\", \"owl\"), (\"fox\", \"owl\")],\n    directed=True,\n)\n\n(\n    web.set_edge_attrs(\"difference\", web.trophic_differences())\n    .get_edge_df(labels=True)\n    .select(\"source\", \"target\", \"difference\")\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (6, 3)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>source</th><th>target</th><th>difference</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;grass&quot;</td><td>&quot;rabbit&quot;</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;grass&quot;</td><td>&quot;mouse&quot;</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;rabbit&quot;</td><td>&quot;fox&quot;</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;mouse&quot;</td><td>&quot;fox&quot;</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;mouse&quot;</td><td>&quot;owl&quot;</td><td>1.5</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;fox&quot;</td><td>&quot;owl&quot;</td><td>0.5</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Prerequisites that skip a level\n\nIn `courses()`, 12 of the 19 prerequisites climb exactly one level. Of the rest, Algorithms\n(CS201) needs both Introduction to Programming (CS101) and Data Structures (CS102),\nwhich itself needs CS101, so one of its edges climbs 1.33 levels and the other only\n0.33. Probability and Statistics (STAT201), at level 4, is required by two 300-level\ncourses that it barely climbs to:\n\n::: {#59b29498 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport polars as pl\n\ncourses = ec.courses().layout_multipartite(subset_key=\"level\")\ndifferences = courses.trophic_differences()\ncourses = courses.set_edge_attrs(\"difference\", differences)\n\n(\n    courses.get_edge_df(labels=True)\n    .filter(pl.col(\"difference\") != 1)\n    .select(\"source\", \"target\", \"difference\")\n    .sort(\"difference\")\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (7, 3)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>source</th><th>target</th><th>difference</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;STAT201&quot;</td><td>&quot;CS360&quot;</td><td>0.166667</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;CS102&quot;</td><td>&quot;CS201&quot;</td><td>0.333333</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;STAT201&quot;</td><td>&quot;CS350&quot;</td><td>0.5</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;CS101&quot;</td><td>&quot;CS201&quot;</td><td>1.333333</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;MATH150&quot;</td><td>&quot;CS201&quot;</td><td>1.333333</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;CS250&quot;</td><td>&quot;CS350&quot;</td><td>1.5</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;CS201&quot;</td><td>&quot;CS360&quot;</td><td>1.833333</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nDrawn with each edge as wide as its difference, with the courses in columns\nby number, the edge from CS201 to Machine Learning (CS360) climbs the most:\n\n::: {#3ef7b7b0 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncourses.plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"dept\", label_by=\"label\",\n    edge_width_by=\"difference\",\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"37.3 14.0 688.8 492.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"37.3\" y=\"14.0\" width=\"688.8\" height=\"492.0\" fill=\"var(--ect-3239c383)\"/>\n<g opacity=\"0.4\"><path d=\"M316.4,424.6 C319.1,415.4 323.8,405.4 332.4,369.1 C340.9,332.8 360.6,237.9 367.6,206.9 C374.6,175.9 373.3,187.1 374.5,183.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4e79a7\" stroke-width=\"4.95\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"383.6,151.4 384.4,185.9 364.6,180.2\" fill=\"#4e79a7\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M316.4,424.6 C319.1,415.4 323.8,405.4 332.4,369.1 C340.9,332.8 359.1,243.2 367.6,206.9 C376.2,170.6 380.9,160.6 383.6,151.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"transparent\" stroke-width=\"8.9\" pointer-events=\"stroke\" data-edge=\"3-10-0\" data-attrs='{\"id\": 14, \"edge\": \"CS201 \\u2192 CS360\", \"difference\": 1.833}'/>\n<g opacity=\"0.4\"><line x1=\"250.3\" y1=\"166.8\" x2=\"280.0\" y2=\"152.0\" stroke=\"#f28e2c\" stroke-width=\"2.9700000000000006\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon 